<h2 id="stop">Stopping the link (runbook, written in E-2)</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Immediately</strong> (Christie, Console): pause <code>reconcileLink</code> and <code>recomputeStatuses</code> in Cloud Scheduler; on Cloud Run <code>ingestmemberupdate</code> → Permissions, remove <code>clayhub-link@</code>'s invoker. (An emergency removal is allowed; granting by hand never is.) Trigger deliveries then fail and Eventarc retries them for up to its retention window; alert emails are rate-limited to one per hour per policy.</li>
  <li><strong>Then</strong> record it: a guarded redeploy of <code>members</code> with <code>invoker: ["private"]</code> (sha phrase), attested.</li>
  <li><strong>To resume</strong>: fix the cause; guarded redeploy with the declared invoker; resume both jobs; Force run <code>reconcileLink</code> to catch up whatever the retries dropped.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Firebase safety checklist</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Every new collection gets an explicit rule and rules tests in the same commit as the code that writes it, deployed before the function (E-2, E-6).</li>
  <li>Writers to my-clay-hub's member data: <code>ingestMemberUpdate</code> (single and reconcile) and <code>recomputeStatuses</code> (status fields only) — both as <code>ingest@</code>, transactions, never deletes.</li>
  <li>Nothing writes to <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>: <code>clayhub-link@</code> holds only get/list; the codebase uses no write API (tested).</li>
  <li>No forbidden field at any nesting level, and no full phone, crosses projects (contract + fixtures); no personal data in logs.</li>
  <li>Emulator tests only; neither guard can reach the other project; the CLI credential file is never read.</li>
  <li>Bulk changes bounded (Q8) and atomic: a stopped reconcile or recompute writes nothing.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Completeness check — if it's interrupted</h2>
<ul>
  <li>E-pre…E-4: docs and code on branches; nothing live until merged and deployed.</li>
  <li>E-5 halfway: Console state is visible; re-read and continue. Nothing uses the accounts until E-6.</li>
  <li>E-6 deployed, E-7 not: ingest is live with no caller — harmless.</li>
  <li>E-7 deployed, E-8 not: triggers send each member whose doc is edited; nothing reads the projection (no sign-in until Phase F); the next scheduled reconcile fills the rest.</li>
  <li>E-7's K13 removal done but delivery unproven: E-8 step 2 is the gate; restore the grant if it fails.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Resume instructions</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Read Status and the newest Decisions-log entry.</li>
  <li>Branches: <code>git -C ~/my-clay-hub branch -a</code>, <code>git -C ~/studio-hub branch -a</code> (names start <code>phase-e-</code>); open PRs and their review state.</li>
  <li>Deploy state: each project's <code>scripts/deploy-functions.sh --status --codebase &lt;cb&gt;</code> (fetch first).</li>
  <li>Reviews: <code>~/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/reviews/my-clay-hub-phase-e-plan-round&lt;n&gt;-*</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="reviews">Reviews</h2>
<h3>Round 1 (Oct 8) — Codex "not ready" (9 blocking); Claude "ready after fixes" (3 blocking)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Finding</th><th>Resolution (v2)</th></tr>
