    86	<tr><td><code>member</code></td><td><code>{memberId, snapshot}</code> or <code>{memberId, tombstone:true}</code>. <code>snapshot</code> is <strong>rebuilt</strong> from allowed keys, never copied and trimmed: <code>name</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>emailLower</code>, <code>stage</code>, <code>memberSince</code>, <code>phoneLast4</code>, <code>retired</code>, <code>scheduledPause: {startDate, endDate} | null</code>, <code>pauseHistory: [{startDate, endDate, priorTerm?}]</code> (legacy <code>start</code>/<code>end</code> mapped to the modern names, the modern value winning as in <code>deriveStatus</code>), <code>scheduledCancellation: {finalAccessDate} | null</code>.</td></tr>
    87	<tr><td>Malformed values</td><td>Never rejected, never carried raw: a string value goes as-is (<code>deriveStatus</code> judges it); a non-string where a date or stage belongs, or a non-object pause, becomes the marker string <code>"!malformed"</code>, which <code>deriveStatus</code> already treats as malformed → <code>review</code>. Tested for each.</td></tr>
    88	<tr><td><code>phoneLast4</code></td><td>The last 4 ASCII digits of <code>phone</code> after removing every non-digit; fewer than 4 digits or no phone → <code>null</code>. Computed in <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>.</td></tr>
    89	<tr><td>Computed on receipt</td><td><code>firstName</code> and <code>lastInitial</code> from <code>name</code>; <code>status</code> from <code>deriveStatus</code>.</td></tr>
    90	<tr><td><code>staff</code></td><td><code>{uid, staff: {name, role, active, grant}}</code> or <code>{uid, tombstone:true}</code>. Sender rule, fail-closed: <code>role</code> must be exactly <code>admin</code>|<code>manager</code>|<code>staff</code>; <code>active</code> a boolean or absent (true); <code>appAccess</code> absent or an array of strings. <code>grant</code> = active and (role is manager/admin, or <code>appAccess</code> contains <code>my-clay-hub</code>). Anything malformed → tombstone + an alert naming the uid only. Never email, PIN or <code>appAccess</code>.</td></tr>
    91	<tr><td><code>reconcile</code></td><td><code>{scope: 'members'|'staff', items: [the same member/staff entries for every live source record]}</code> — the complete set at one readTime. The receiver computes everything (see E-2).</td></tr>
    92	<tr><td>Tombstone (stored)</td><td>Replaces the document: <code>{memberId, tombstone:true, status:'removed', sourceReadTime, updatedAt}</code>; <code>memberProfiles/{memberId}</code> and <code>staffRoster/staff_{uid}</code> likewise. A later live snapshot restores only the allowlist.</td></tr>
    93	<tr><td>Responses</td><td>200 <code>{result: applied|stale|unchanged}</code>; 400 for a malformed envelope; 409 for a reconcile stopped by a threshold; 5xx only for real failures. The sender throws (so retries happen) only on 5xx, 429 and timeouts.</td></tr>
    94	<tr><td>Logging</td><td>Never request bodies, names, emails, phone digits, notes or source documents — only memberId/uid, kind, result and counts.</td></tr>
    95	</table>
    96	
    97	<h2 id="settings">Functions and their settings</h2>
    98	<table>
    99	<tr><th>Function</th><th>Project / codebase</th><th>Trigger</th><th>Runs as</th><th>Settings</th></tr>
   100	<tr><td><code>ingestMemberUpdate</code></td><td>my-clay-hub / <code>members</code></td><td>https, invoker <code>clayhub-link@tinker-hq-apps</code></td><td><code>ingest@</code></td><td>timeout 120 s (a reconcile is one call of at most 500 writes), memory 512MiB, cpu 1, concurrency 10, maxInstances 3</td></tr>
   101	<tr><td><code>recomputeStatuses</code></td><td>my-clay-hub / <code>members</code></td><td>schedule <code>every day 09:30</code> UTC; retryCount 2, maxRetrySeconds 0, minBackoff 600, maxBackoff 1200, maxDoublings 1</td><td><code>ingest@</code></td><td>timeout 300 s, memory 256MiB, maxInstances 1, concurrency 1</td></tr>
   102	<tr><td><code>onClayHubMemberWritten</code></td><td>tinker-hq-apps / <code>clayhub-link</code></td><td>Firestore <code>document.written</code> on <code>clayHub_members/{docId}</code>, <code>(default)</code>, nam5, retry true</td><td><code>clayhub-link@</code></td><td>timeout 60 s, memory 256MiB, maxInstances 5</td></tr>
   103	<tr><td><code>onStaffUserWritten</code></td><td>tinker-hq-apps / <code>clayhub-link</code></td><td>Firestore <code>document.written</code> on <code>users/{uid}</code>, retry true</td><td><code>clayhub-link@</code></td><td>as above</td></tr>
   104	<tr><td><code>reconcileLink</code></td><td>tinker-hq-apps / <code>clayhub-link</code></td><td>schedule <code>every 6 hours from 01:15 to 19:15</code> UTC (01:15, 07:15, 13:15, 19:15); retryCount 1, maxRetrySeconds 0, minBackoff 600, maxBackoff 600, maxDoublings 0</td><td><code>clayhub-link@</code></td><td>timeout 300 s, memory 512MiB, maxInstances 1, concurrency 1</td></tr>
   105	</table>
   106	<p class="note">Exact values are reviewed in E-2/E-4's PRs; the guard refuses anything that differs from the declaration. The ingest URL is a hard-coded constant in the sender, tested.</p>
