   134	<div class="phase">
   135	<h3>E-2 — my-clay-hub: the receiving side (codebase <code>members</code>) <span class="status-tag not-ready">execution-ready: false</span></h3>
   136	<ul>
   137	  <li><strong><code>ingestMemberUpdate</code></strong> (settings above). <code>member</code>/<code>staff</code>: one transaction — read the target doc(s), apply the readTime gate, derive status from the stored source shape, write <code>members</code> and <code>memberProfiles</code> together (or <code>staffRoster</code>), or replace them with tombstones.</li>
   138	  <li><strong><code>reconcile</code></strong> (one call): validate the whole batch first; read every target; work out the effective change set after the readTime gate (additions, updates, status changes, removals = held live records absent from the batch); apply Q8's thresholds (denominator = live records held; additions don't count; the first fill into an empty collection is exempt); if it passes, write everything in one transaction (≤ 500 writes; refuse above that with an alert — far beyond today's size); if not, write nothing, answer 409, log the counts. Staff the same.</li>
   139	  <li><strong><code>recomputeStatuses</code></strong> (09:30 UTC): a dry run over every live member first (Q8 threshold → stop, nothing written); then per member a transaction that re-reads the doc and re-derives from its current stored source shape, writing <code>members.status</code> and <code>memberProfiles.status</code> together only if it changed. An ingest landing in between is never overwritten, because the transaction re-reads.</li>
   140	  <li><strong><code>firestore.rules</code></strong>: explicit deny-all blocks for <code>members</code>, <code>memberProfiles</code>, <code>staffRoster</code> with rules tests (no sign-in exists until Phase F, which adds a member's own-profile read). These deploy through the rules guard <em>before</em> the function.</li>
   141	  <li>Declarations, iam-expectations (<code>ingest@</code> and its custom role), and a FUNCTIONS-ROLLBACK section including the stop/resume runbook (below).</li>
   142	</ul>
   143	<p><strong>Tests first</strong> (emulator, Node 22): every fixture; the readTime gate (earlier, equal, same millisecond with different nanos, malformed); tombstone replaces all former personal data, re-appearance restores only the allowlist; every D4 row through the real <code>deriveStatus</code>, including <code>priorTerm</code> and each malformed value → <code>review</code>; reconcile: first fill exempt, exact threshold boundaries, small denominators, additions, already-tombstoned members, a stale item inside a batch, a stop leaving both collections untouched; recompute vs ingest in both orders, threshold stop with zero writes, tombstones excluded, profile kept in step; staff: unticking and demotion tombstone, a malformed role never grants; rules deny every client operation; no log line contains a fixture's name, email or phone.</p>
