   227	
   228	<h2 id="stop">Stopping the link (runbook, written in E-2)</h2>
   229	<ol>
   230	  <li><strong>Immediately</strong> (Christie, Console): pause <code>reconcileLink</code> and <code>recomputeStatuses</code> in Cloud Scheduler; on Cloud Run <code>ingestmemberupdate</code> → Permissions, remove <code>clayhub-link@</code>'s invoker. (An emergency removal is allowed; granting by hand never is.) Trigger deliveries then fail and Eventarc retries them for up to its retention window; alert emails are rate-limited to one per hour per policy.</li>
   231	  <li><strong>Then</strong> record it: a guarded redeploy of <code>members</code> with <code>invoker: ["private"]</code> (sha phrase), attested.</li>
   232	  <li><strong>To resume</strong>: fix the cause; guarded redeploy with the declared invoker; resume both jobs; Force run <code>reconcileLink</code> to catch up whatever the retries dropped.</li>
   233	</ol>
   234	
   235	<h2>Firebase safety checklist</h2>
   236	<ul>
   237	  <li>Every new collection gets an explicit rule and rules tests in the same commit as the code that writes it, deployed before the function (E-2, E-6).</li>
   238	  <li>Writers to my-clay-hub's member data: <code>ingestMemberUpdate</code> (single and reconcile) and <code>recomputeStatuses</code> (status fields only) — both as <code>ingest@</code>, transactions, never deletes.</li>
   239	  <li>Nothing writes to <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>: <code>clayhub-link@</code> holds only get/list; the codebase uses no write API (tested).</li>
   240	  <li>No forbidden field at any nesting level, and no full phone, crosses projects (contract + fixtures); no personal data in logs.</li>
   241	  <li>Emulator tests only; neither guard can reach the other project; the CLI credential file is never read.</li>
   242	  <li>Bulk changes bounded (Q8) and atomic: a stopped reconcile or recompute writes nothing.</li>
   243	</ul>
   244	
   245	<h2>Completeness check — if it's interrupted</h2>
   246	<ul>
   247	  <li>E-pre…E-4: docs and code on branches; nothing live until merged and deployed.</li>
   248	  <li>E-5 halfway: Console state is visible; re-read and continue. Nothing uses the accounts until E-6.</li>
   249	  <li>E-6 deployed, E-7 not: ingest is live with no caller — harmless.</li>
   250	  <li>E-7 deployed, E-8 not: triggers send each member whose doc is edited; nothing reads the projection (no sign-in until Phase F); the next scheduled reconcile fills the rest.</li>
   251	  <li>E-7's K13 removal done but delivery unproven: E-8 step 2 is the gate; restore the grant if it fails.</li>
   252	</ul>
   253	
   254	<h2>Resume instructions</h2>
   255	<ul>
   256	  <li>Read Status and the newest Decisions-log entry.</li>
   257	  <li>Branches: <code>git -C ~/my-clay-hub branch -a</code>, <code>git -C ~/studio-hub branch -a</code> (names start <code>phase-e-</code>); open PRs and their review state.</li>
   258	  <li>Deploy state: each project's <code>scripts/deploy-functions.sh --status --codebase &lt;cb&gt;</code> (fetch first).</li>
   259	  <li>Reviews: <code>~/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/reviews/my-clay-hub-phase-e-plan-round&lt;n&gt;-*</code>.</li>
   260	</ul>
   261	
   262	<h2 id="reviews">Reviews</h2>
   263	<h3>Round 1 (Oct 8) — Codex "not ready" (9 blocking); Claude "ready after fixes" (3 blocking)</h3>
   264	<table>
   265	<tr><th>Finding</th><th>Resolution (v2)</th></tr>
   266	<tr><td>The 10%/5% stops can't work from the sender, a partial reconcile isn't atomic, the first fill would trip them (both, blocking)</td><td>The <code>reconcile</code> kind: the receiver computes the whole change set and writes all-or-nothing; denominators defined; first fill exempt; Q8 floors.</td></tr>
   267	<tr><td>Nested notes/billing would leak; strict validation would hide malformed values from <code>deriveStatus</code> (both, blocking)</td><td>The contract: snapshots rebuilt from allowed keys at every level; malformed values carried as <code>"!malformed"</code>; fixtures for each.</td></tr>
   268	<tr><td>readTime has no wire format; same-millisecond reads collapse (both)</td><td>{seconds, nanos}, stored as a Timestamp, compared as a pair; tests.</td></tr>
   269	<tr><td>Staff input must fail closed; F5 overstated the schema (Codex, blocking; Claude should-fix)</td><td>The staff rule in the contract; F5 corrected; tests.</td></tr>
   270	<tr><td>K13 relies on an unproven delivery identity; a code search isn't a workload audit (Codex, blocking)</td><td>E-5 inventory and audit logs; E-8 step 2 proves delivery after the removal; Q3 rewritten.</td></tr>
   271	<tr><td>The E-6 OIDC probe had no mechanism; the synthetic member (Codex, blocking; Claude should-fix)</td><td>Dropped: E-6 proves 403 and the invoker reading; the first authenticated call is E-8's logged first fill.</td></tr>
   272	<tr><td>The stop procedure is refused by the guard (both)</td><td>"Stopping the link": Console pause + invoker removal, then a guarded <code>["private"]</code> redeploy.</td></tr>
   273	<tr><td>Decisions and gates too late (Codex, blocking)</td><td>E-pre; E-7 lists every gate, including #64; E-8 adds a fresh vault copy.</td></tr>
   274	<tr><td>Recompute needs atomicity and race handling (Codex, blocking)</td><td>Dry run, then per-member transactions re-reading; profiles in step; tests both orders.</td></tr>
   275	<tr><td>Adding functions to studio-hub can break the rules guard (Claude, blocking)</td><td>E-3: rules guard untouched, functions suites outside <code>npm test</code>, an isolation test, a dry rules <code>--status</code>/<code>--diff</code>.</td></tr>
