   155	# D-4 (F13 amended for schedules, V3): a function is HTTP (httpsTrigger) or scheduled (scheduleTrigger), as its
   156	# declaration says; every other trigger kind is still refused by name. A declaration's key set is exact. A schedule's
   157	# schedule, time zone (UTC only) and all five retry values are numbers/strings EQUAL to its declaration — an unset
   158	# value (absent, or null) refuses, because the CLI never clears a retry setting removed from code (J5).
